# The density matrix and the Bloch sphere. A single qubit's state is a point in the Bloch ball: pure states sit on the
# surface at radius one, mixed states inside, and the maximally mixed state, knowing nothing, at the center. The two
# antipodal points on the surface are the orthogonal states, the poles being the computational basis, and reflecting a
# pure state through the center sends it to the orthogonal one. This file MODELS the two poles of the Bloch sphere and
# DEFINES the antipodal map that exchanges them, then PROVES it is an involution, so the poles are a matched orthogonal
# pair. The purity of the maximally mixed qubit, one half, and the trace-one normalization are recorded as machine-integer
# facts in scaled units. The antipodal involution is proved over the actual pole type by induction.

# The two poles of the Bloch sphere, the orthogonal computational-basis states.
form pole
  case north
  case south

# The antipodal map, reflecting a pure state through the center of the Bloch ball to the orthogonal state, exchanging the
# two poles.
task antipode
  take p, like pole
  like pole
  fork case, read p
    case north
      send back
        make south
    case south
      send back
        make north

# THE ANTIPODAL MAP IS AN INVOLUTION: reflecting twice returns the state, antipode (antipode p) = p, for every pole, so
# the two poles are a matched pair of orthogonal states. Proved by induction over the two poles.
rule the-antipodal-map-is-an-involution
  seat p, like pole
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call antipode
        call antipode
          read p
      read p
  fold p

# THE POLES ARE ORTHOGONAL: the antipode of the north pole is the south pole, antipode north = south, the two orthogonal
# basis states at opposite ends of the Bloch sphere.
rule the-poles-are-orthogonal
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call antipode
        make north
      make south
  calm hold

# THE MAXIMALLY MIXED QUBIT has trace one, its two eigenvalues each one half summing to the whole, in half-units
# 1 + 1 = 2, as a machine-integer fact.
hold density-matrix-trace-is-one
  call is-equal
    code 2
    call add
      code 1
      code 1

# PURITY ORDERS PURE ABOVE MIXED: a pure state has purity one, the maximally mixed qubit one half, so in quarter-units the
# pure four is above the mixed two, 4 above 2.
hold pure-is-purer-than-mixed
  call is-above
    code 4
    code 2
